            <h2>Route Overview: Alexandria to Williamsburg</h2>
            <p>Traveling from <b>Alexandria to Williamsburg</b> by train is a convenient and scenic way to connect Northern Virginia with one of America's most historic colonial destinations. This route provides passengers with a relaxed alternative to driving or flying, especially popular for history enthusiasts, families, students, and weekend trips. While not as fast as high-speed rail in Europe, the Northeast Regional offers comfortable seating, onboard amenities, and spectacular views through Virginia's historic Tidewater region. </p>
            <p>The route is served by Amtrak's Northeast Regional, offering daily departures between Alexandria Union Station and Williamsburg's charming station. Compared to road travel on I-95 and I-64, taking the train helps you avoid highway traffic. It makes city-center to city-center travel easy without worrying about parking or rental cars in Colonial Williamsburg. The Northeast Regional connects Williamsburg to the broader Northeast Corridor, making it easy to reach destinations like Washington, D.C., Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York, and Boston. </p>
